<!--
  PHPMD baseline — RETAINED, not deleted, and DELIBERATELY SMALLER.

  Part of the fleet suppression audit (ConductionNL/.github#155). Measured with
  PHPMD 2.15.0 / PHP 8.4.22, exit code read directly:

      reported with this baseline      0
      baseline deleted, before the PR  99   (what the 56 old entries hid)
      baseline deleted, after the PR   65

  The 34 findings that are gone were FIXED (all MissingImport), not
  re-baselined; their seven entries are removed below, so the gate genuinely
  covers those files again. Deleting an entry whose finding no longer exists is
  the point: a file-scoped entry (one with no `method` attribute) suppresses
  EVERY future finding of that rule in that file, so a stale entry is a dead
  gate, not a harmless leftover. That is also why 56 entries were hiding 99
  findings rather than 56.

  Separately, 32 UnusedFormalParameter findings in lib/Migration are no longer
  suppressed by four blanket @SuppressWarnings docblocks but by
  phpmd-unusedparams.xml, a second ruleset holding that ONE rule with a
  TOP-LEVEL exclude-pattern. Those 32 are interface-mandated:
  OCP\Migration\IMigrationStep fixes the changeSchema / preSchemaChange /
  postSchemaChange signatures, so a step that needs none of the parameters
  still cannot drop them. The exclusion is deliberately NOT applied to the main
  ruleset - that would drop lib/Migration from every rule and swallow the real
  ExcessiveMethodLength finding in Version6Date20241011085015.

  WHAT REMAINS (65 findings, 49 entries) and why the file is still here:

  * 21 ElseExpression, 11 CyclomaticComplexity, 6 NPathComplexity,
    6 ExcessiveMethodLength, 5 ExcessiveClassComplexity, 2 StaticAccess,
    2 LongVariable, 2 ErrorControlOperator, 2 CouplingBetweenObjects,
    1 ExcessiveParameterList, 1 ExcessiveClassLength — genuine, fixable debt.
  * 6 UnusedFormalParameter OUTSIDE lib/Migration (WooController, OoapiService,
    WooService) — NOT interface-mandated, and not covered by the Migration
    exclusion. Genuine debt.

  Each remaining fix is a behaviour-bearing refactor. This repo's unit suite
  needs a Nextcloud server tree plus openregister to run, so those refactors
  need CI to verify them and were out of scope for this pass.

  Deleting this file today would redden `development` for everyone with 65 real
  findings, which helps nobody. It stays until the remainder is burned down.

  This baseline is a RATCHET: any NEW violation outside these entries fails the
  gate. Do NOT regenerate it to silence a new finding, and do NOT re-add an
  entry that a fix has retired.
-->
